We also need to ensure we refer to the list before addition. Use \old(this.get(i)). Note that after addition, size increased by 1, but indices before index should be same.

Thus assert: (index >=0 && index <= \old(this.size())) && role != null => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; ( (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i))) );

But role is a parameter, not a field; we cannot refer to role after method (maybe still accessible). In spec we can refer to role variable.

Thus final assert.

